- src/lib/stop-intelligence.ts: pure deriveStopVisit() — walks a trip's
  own gps_pings trail (already collected in Phase 3) and finds when the
  agent crossed a stop's geofence (route_points.geofence_radius_m,
  falling back to mcc_centres.default_geofence_radius_m — no hard-coded
  radius). Requires 2 consecutive fixes on each side of the crossing to
  absorb GPS jitter, and ignores 'unavailable'-quality fixes rather than
  treating them as exact (Phase 3 rule).
- useLiveOps.ts: route_points select now includes geofence_radius_m;
  milk_collections select now includes trip_id/route_point_id/
  distance_from_point_m (no new table — existing collection records are
  reused, not duplicated, per the plan).
- live.tsx: new 'Current stop' panel in Agent Detail — Arrived /
  Collection completed (from milk_collections, matched by trip_id +
  route_point_id) / Departed / Stop duration / Travel time to reach
  (from the previous stop's derived departure, or trip start for the
  first stop).

No new DB migration this phase — every field needed (geofence_radius_m,
default_geofence_radius_m, trip_id, route_point_id, distance_from_point_m)
already existed. Deliberately independent of trip.tsx's existing 'arrive'
mutation (a manual 'View farmers' tap, not a location signal) and never
touches milk_collections — GPS provides context only, the collection
stays a separate transaction.
